INT. CRANE & SONS FUNERAL HOME - VIEWING ROOM B - DAY

A deposition in a room meant for mourning. Folding tables have been set among potted lilies. An empty casket stands on a draped bier at the head of the room, lid open, lined with white satin. Soft organ music leaks from a ceiling speaker no one can find the switch for.

BARNABAS FLINT, fifties, plaintiff's counsel, sits at the near table with a stack of exhibits. ROSAMUND ACHEBE, forties, defence counsel, sits across from him, calm as a priest. At the head of the table, HOLLIS DUNMORE, sixties, the witness, a retired claims adjuster in a navy blazer, lowers himself into a funeral parlour armchair. JUNO PAREKH, twenties, the videographer, hunches behind her tripod. LEOPOLD ISHIGURO, fifties, the court reporter, sets up his steno machine by the casket. MR. SELWYN CRANE, seventies, funeral director, hovers in the doorway with a box of tissues.

BARNABAS
Mr. Dunmore, I'm going to ask you to identify Exhibit Twelve.

HOLLIS
Of course.

ROSAMUND
Objection. Foundation.

BARNABAS
He wrote it.

ROSAMUND
He hasn't said that.

HOLLIS
I wrote it.

ROSAMUND
Don't help him, Mr. Dunmore.

HOLLIS
I'm only saying.

BARNABAS
Please read the highlighted line.

HOLLIS
"Claim denied pursuant to section nine."

JUNO
(from behind the tripod)
Sorry, can you speak up?

HOLLIS
"Claim denied pursuant to section nine."

LEOPOLD
Section nine or section "nine-dash-b"?

HOLLIS
Nine.

BARNABAS
And what is section nine?

ROSAMUND
Objection. Calls for a legal conclusion.

SELWYN
(from the door, softly)
Forgive me. Would anyone like a tissue?

BARNABAS
No, thank you, Mr. Crane.

ROSAMUND
Not at present.

HOLLIS
I'll take one.

Selwyn glides in, sets the box beside Hollis, and glides out. Juno steps from behind the tripod to adjust the lens and trips on a lily pot. Leopold catches the pot. Barnabas and Rosamund both reach for the water pitcher at once; their hands knock it over, and a flood runs across the exhibits. Hollis grabs his own copy and holds it above his head like a man fording a river.

ROSAMUND
Barnabas, that's my notes!

BARNABAS
It's my exhibit!

LEOPOLD
Can we go off the record?

JUNO
I'm still rolling.

HOLLIS
Does anyone have a towel?

SELWYN
(returning, with an armload of black linen)
Our finest.

They mop in silence. The organ swells. Water drips off the casket's satin.

BARNABAS
(wringing a page)
Let's resume.
